<title>TURKEY: Rebel Kurds kidnap 10 villagers.</title>
<headline>Rebel Kurds kidnap 10 villagers.</headline>
<dateline>DIYARBAKIR 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten villagers from Turkey's southeast have been abducted by rebel Kurds, security officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Kurdistan Workers Party (PKK) guerrillas took the villagers from Uzungecit in Sirnak province on Wednesday evening, officials said.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>More than 25,000 people have died in the 12 year of conflict between troops and the PKK guerrillas, who are fighting for autonomy or independence in the mainly Kurdish southeast.</p>
</text>
